     "text": [
      "=== ABLATION COMPARISON: 11-segment vs 20-segment ===\n",
      "Subjects with valid ('ok') results in OLD (11-seg): 26\n",
      "Subjects with valid ('ok') results in NEW (20-seg): 26\n",
      "Paired subjects (present + 'ok' in BOTH): 26\n",
      "\n",
      "--- Accuracy (n=26 paired subjects) ---\n",
      "  Mean OLD:  0.4589 (+-0.0807)\n",
      "  Mean NEW:  0.4721 (+-0.1021)\n",
      "  Mean delta (NEW-OLD): +0.0132\n",
      "  Paired t-test:   t(25) = 1.2820, p = 0.2116\n",
      "  Wilcoxon signed-rank: W = 134.0, p = 0.3032\n",
      "  Cohen's d (paired): 0.2514\n",
      "\n",
      "--- Kappa (n=26 paired subjects) ---\n",
      "  Mean OLD:  0.1888 (+-0.1208)\n",
      "  Mean NEW:  0.2079 (+-0.1529)\n",
      "  Mean delta (NEW-OLD): +0.0191\n",
      "  Paired t-test:   t(25) = 1.2309, p = 0.2298\n",
      "  Wilcoxon signed-rank: W = 136.0, p = 0.3276\n",
      "  Cohen's d (paired): 0.2414\n",
      "\n",
      "NOTE: branch-accuracy/fusion-weight fields not present in both JSONs (likely the OLD 11-segment run predates that logging addition) -- skipping branch-level statistical comparison.\n",
      "\n",
      "==============================================================================\n",
      "PER-SUBJECT DIRECTION OF CHANGE (accuracy)\n",
      "==============================================================================\n",
      "Improved (20-seg > 11-seg): 16/26\n",
      "Worse    (20-seg < 11-seg): 10/26\n",
      "Unchanged:                  0/26\n",
      "\n",
      "Full per-subject comparison table saved: E:\\kntu\\Thesis\\codes\\Results\\TSFNET_PAPER_EXACT_nback_20SEG_ABLATION\\ablation_11seg_vs_20seg_comparison.csv\n",
      "\n",
      "--- Thesis-ready paragraph (Ablation Study section) ---\n",
      "To formally test whether extending the fNIRS segment count from 11 (paper-exact, [-2,10]s window) to 20 (extended, [-2,42]s window, covering the full hemodynamic response including the post-peak undershoot) improved classification performance, a paired comparison was performed across all 26 subjects with valid results under both conditions. Mean subject-level accuracy increased from 45.89% (11-segment) to 47.21% (20-segment), a mean paired improvement of +1.32 percentage points (paired t-test: t(25)=1.28, p = 0.212; Wilcoxon signed-rank: W=134.0, p = 0.303; Cohen's d=0.25, a small effect). Cohen's kappa showed a corresponding increase from 0.189 to 0.208 (+0.019; t(25)=1.23, p = 0.230; W=136.0, p = 0.328). 16 of 26 subjects (62%) showed improved accuracy under the extended-window condition.\n",
      "\n",
      "Paragraph saved: E:\\kntu\\Thesis\\codes\\Results\\TSFNET_PAPER_EXACT_nback_20SEG_ABLATION\\ablation_11seg_vs_20seg_paragraph.txt\n",
      "Statistical test summary saved: E:\\kntu\\Thesis\\codes\\Results\\TSFNET_PAPER_EXACT_nback_20SEG_ABLATION\\ablation_statistical_tests_summary.csv\n"
     ]
    }
